{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 requires implementing a `solve(case)` function that performs grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree.\n\nKey rules from the candidate_artifact:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure from the nodes list\n2. Process nodes from deepest to shallowest (considering depth first, then node ID as tiebreak)\n3. For each node (in that order), check if it can be removed:\n   - Must be `removable: true`\n   - Not root\n   - Not a required symbol\n   - No retained children\n   - After removal, all required symbols must still be represented\n4. Track removal order\n5. Return retained IDs (sorted) and removed IDs (in removal order)\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n- Nodes:\n  - root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=\"root\"\n  - n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=\"s1\"\n  - n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=\"s2\"\n  - n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=\"s0\"\n  - n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=\"s1\", parent=n2\n  - n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=\"s2\", parent=n3\n  - n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=\"s0\", parent=n1\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcess order (deepest first, then by node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- Depth 0: root\n\nProcessing n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=\"s1\", parent=n2):\n- Check: no retained children (leaf node)\n- Check: required symbols after removal: \"root\" still represented by root, \"s1\" still represented by n1 → OK\n- Remove n4\n\nProcessing n5 (depth=2, removable=false):\n- Cannot remove (removable=false)\n\nProcessing n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=\"s0\", parent=n1):\n- Check: no retained children (leaf node)\n- Check: required symbols after removal: \"root\" represented by root, \"s1\" represented by n1 → OK\n- Remove n6\n\nProcessing n1 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Cannot remove (removable=false)\n\nProcessing n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=\"s2\", parent=root):\n- Check: no retained children (n4 was removed, so n2 has no retained children) → OK\n- Check: required symbols after removal: \"root\" represented by root, \"s1\" represented by n1 → OK\n- Remove n2\n\nProcessing n3 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Cannot remove\n\nProcessing root (removable=false):\n- Cannot remove\n\nRemoved: n4, n6, n2\nRetained: root, n1, n3, n5\n\nLet me verify: retained_node_ids sorted = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\nremoved_node_ids (in order) = [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n\nNow let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deepest first, then by node ID as tiebreak\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if already removed (shouldn't happen but safety check)\n        if nid not in retained:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: node has no retained children\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols still represented\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        remaining_symbols = {node_map[r][\"symbol\"] for r in retained}\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\n            # Keep removed\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Restore\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, let me re-check the \"retained children\" condition. When we process a node, its children might have already been removed. So we need to check if any children are still in `retained`.\n\nYes, my implementation already does that: `if any(child in retained for child in children[nid])`.\n\nLet me trace through case 0 again with my implementation:\n\nInitial retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\n\nsorted_nodes order: depth 2 first (n4, n5, n6), then depth 1 (n1, n2, n3), then depth 0 (root)\n\nWait, within same depth, sort by node ID. Let me check: \"n4\", \"n5\", \"n6\" - string sort gives n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6. \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\" - n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3. That seems fine.\n\nBut wait, \"root\" vs \"n1\" etc. - string comparison: \"n\" \u003c \"r\" so all nX come before \"root\". But root is depth 0, so it's processed last anyway.\n\nProcessing n4 (removable=true, symbol=\"s1\"):\n- children of n4: [] (none)\n- retained.discard(\"n4\") → retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6}\n- remaining_symbols = {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s2\", \"s0\", \"s2\", \"s0\"} = {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s2\", \"s0\"}\n- required_symbols {\"root\", \"s1\"} ⊆ {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s2\", \"s0\"} → True\n- Keep removed, removed_order = [\"n4\"]\n\nProcessing n5 (removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nProcessing n6 (removable=true, symbol=\"s0\"):\n- children of n6: [] (none)\n- retained.discard(\"n6\") → retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5}\n- remaining_symbols from {root, n1, n2, n3, n5} = {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s2\", \"s0\", \"s2\"} = {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s2\", \"s0\"}\n- required {\"root\", \"s1\"} ⊆ remaining → True\n- Keep removed, removed_order = [\"n4\", \"n6\"]\n\nProcessing n1 (removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nProcessing n2 (removable=true, symbol=\"s2\"):\n- children of n2: [\"n4\"] - but n4 is not in retained → no retained children\n- retained.discard(\"n2\") → retained = {root, n1, n3, n5}\n- remaining_symbols from {root, n1, n3, n5} = {\"root\", \"s1\", \"s0\", \"s2\"}\n- required {\"root\", \"s1\"} ⊆ remaining → True\n- Keep removed, removed_order = [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n\nProcessing n3 (removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nProcessing root (removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nFinal: retained = {root, n1, n3, n5}\nretained_sorted = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\nremoved_order = [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n\nThat looks correct.\n\nNow let me write the final implementation as a JSON string properly escaped.\n\nThe implementation looks good. Let me write the final JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained set\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Process deepest first, stable tie-break by node ID string\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Must still be in retained (safety)\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Must have no retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove and check required symbols still covered\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        remaining_symbols = {node_map[r][\\\"symbol\\\"] for r in retained}\\n\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            # Restore — removal would break coverage\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01UcN4MeSxC87tkyi2wmAiku","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2436},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2436,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":26,"output_tokens":2560,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2132},"service_tier":"standard"}}